   "name": "South Street Local Historic District",
   "status": "settled",
   "summary": "In 2022, the Historic District Commission initiated discussions and hired consultant Chris Skelly to prepare strategies and a Chapter 40C study report for a proposed local historic district along South Street highlighting the area's shipbuilding heritage. The commission refined boundaries, developed educational brochures, conducted outreach at Medford PorchFest, and held public hearings. In early 2024, the Historical Commission voted to support the district's creation as it advanced to the Planning Board and City Council. By late 2024, the district reached completion pending final filing of the district map with the Registry of Deeds, followed by site visits in 2025 to plan permanent neighborhood signage.",
