  {
   "name": "Thomas Brooks Park and Pomp's Wall preservation",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "The Historical Commission oversaw multi-phase restoration and archaeological work at Thomas Brooks Park beginning with volunteer digs in 2022 and community discussions to rename the fieldstone wall as Pomp's Wall in honor of its enslaved builder. Phase One work completed masonry repairs on Pomp's Wall and the Grove Street fieldstone wall using Community Preservation Act funds. Landscape architect Peter Hedlund presented conceptual designs for later phases, including ADA-accessible pathways, interpretive signage, and foundation surface markers. The commission secured Phase Two funding for tree trimming, signage, and archaeological capping with SWCA, holding public meetings to gather abutters' input and continuing artifact cleaning and site maintenance through 2026.",
