  {
   "name": "Cross Street Cemetery restoration and archaeology",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "The commission undertook long-term preservation efforts for the Cross Street Cemetery, starting with initial funding for headstone foundation fieldwork and historical records research. Exploratory trenching conducted by PAL at the former cemetery parcel uncovered artifacts and human remains, prompting state coordination and plans for exhumation beneath the City Hall upper parking lot. In addition to assessing relocated headstones at Oak Grove Cemetery and funding pilot veteran headstone restorations, the commission sought Community Preservation Act grants to clean walls and recreate entrance gates. Through 2026, the commission issued RFPs for headstone conservation and prepared ground-penetrating radar investigations.",
