  {
   "name": "Historic district certificates of appropriateness and design guidelines",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "The Historic District Commission reviews applications for exterior alterations, fences, and additions on properties within Medford's local historic districts. In 2023, the commission drafted and unanimously approved comprehensive Medford Historic District Design Guidelines that established standards for replacement materials, roofing, windows, and additions while accommodating modern materials that resemble historic features. The commission subsequently adjudicated applications under these guidelines, including window replacements at 15 and 20 Hillside Avenue. It also reviewed and approved plans for a new carriage house accessory dwelling unit at 21 Touro Avenue and organized educational presentations regarding cellular PVC millwork and historic property insurance.",
