  {
   "name": "Municipal zoning reform and preservation incentives",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "The commission monitored and engaged with citywide zoning and planning initiatives to advocate for historic protections and streamline demolition reviews. Members studied neighboring municipal bylaws, such as Reading's preservation zoning ordinance, and drafted potential local amendments to fast-track minor outbuildings or automate significance for pre-1900 structures. Both commissions tracked state housing legislation, formally voting to oppose Senate Bill S.993 over concerns that it would diminish local oversight of historic carriage houses and outbuildings. The Historical Commission actively participated in Medford Square and Boston Avenue rezoning discussions, advocating for dimensional waivers and design incentives in exchange for preserving historic structures.",
